1
00:00:01,200 --> 00:00:03,998
A critical C V E lands at four in

2
00:00:03,998 --> 00:00:07,982
the afternoon. The permanent fix is weeks away.

3
00:00:07,982 --> 00:00:09,678
The exposure is now.

4
00:00:12,678 --> 00:00:15,896
What if an agent could draft the interim mitigation,

5
00:00:15,896 --> 00:00:17,691
test it against real traffic,

6
00:00:17,691 --> 00:00:20,414
and have an approval package on your desk by

7
00:00:20,414 --> 00:00:22,332
five? That is virtual patching,

8
00:00:22,332 --> 00:00:24,189
done with agents, done safely.

9
00:00:27,188 --> 00:00:31,859
Gennoor Tech presents the Agentic Virtual Patching Platform.

10
00:00:34,859 --> 00:00:37,323
One finding in. One tested patch out.

11
00:00:37,323 --> 00:00:40,121
You build the platform in nine increments,

12
00:00:40,121 --> 00:00:43,185
and every increment is something you can test,

13
00:00:43,185 --> 00:00:46,782
review and demonstrate. Claude drafts the code and the

14
00:00:46,782 --> 00:00:49,912
tests. You inspect the diffs and run the suite.

15
00:00:49,912 --> 00:00:51,778
Nothing is accepted blindly.

16
00:00:54,778 --> 00:00:57,675
You start with what a virtual patch really is.

17
00:00:57,675 --> 00:01:00,635
An interim mitigation at the enforcement point,

18
00:01:00,635 --> 00:01:03,218
never a substitute for the permanent fix.

19
00:01:03,218 --> 00:01:04,541
You stand up the lab,

20
00:01:04,541 --> 00:01:07,690
a deliberately vulnerable endpoint behind a proxy,

21
00:01:07,690 --> 00:01:09,706
and you write the product brief.

22
00:01:12,706 --> 00:01:17,212
Then ingestion. A typed vulnerability record with advisory I

23
00:01:17,212 --> 00:01:21,193
D, affected component, endpoint, evidence references,

24
00:01:21,193 --> 00:01:25,775
confidence and source timestamp. A mock scanner importer that

25
00:01:25,775 --> 00:01:29,531
validates its schema and reports what it rejected.

26
00:01:29,531 --> 00:01:34,188
And a context collector that never infers reachability without

27
00:01:34,188 --> 00:01:34,864
evidence.

28
00:01:37,864 --> 00:01:39,939
On day two the agent arrives.

29
00:01:39,939 --> 00:01:44,018
A mitigation planning agent that summarizes the issue and

30
00:01:44,018 --> 00:01:47,310
proposes a strategy from an approved playbook.

31
00:01:47,310 --> 00:01:50,102
It must cite the evidence it was given,

32
00:01:50,102 --> 00:01:52,893
and it must mark what it does not know.

33
00:01:55,893 --> 00:01:59,411
Candidate rules are generated only through approved,

34
00:01:59,411 --> 00:02:02,117
versioned templates and a strict schema.

35
00:02:02,117 --> 00:02:05,229
Ask it for an arbitrary proxy directive and it

36
00:02:05,229 --> 00:02:07,935
refuses. That constraint is the product.

37
00:02:10,935 --> 00:02:12,962
Then the part most teams skip.

38
00:02:12,962 --> 00:02:16,340
A real test harness. Positive tests for the target

39
00:02:16,340 --> 00:02:19,313
case. Benign traffic that must keep flowing.

40
00:02:19,313 --> 00:02:24,245
Regression tests. And bypass variants that challenge simplistic matching.

41
00:02:24,245 --> 00:02:27,353
The validation gate fails closed when a run is

42
00:02:27,353 --> 00:02:30,731
incomplete, and you will watch it do exactly that.

43
00:02:33,731 --> 00:02:36,500
Day three is approval and operations.

44
00:02:36,500 --> 00:02:38,744
A review bundle with the diff,

45
00:02:38,744 --> 00:02:40,839
the test results, the owner,

46
00:02:40,839 --> 00:02:44,879
an expiry date, the rollback command and the approver.

47
00:02:44,879 --> 00:02:48,620
Deployment goes only to lab staging and only after

48
00:02:48,620 --> 00:02:51,912
a person says yes. You then run the rollback

49
00:02:51,912 --> 00:02:54,680
drill and write the operator runbook.

50
00:02:57,680 --> 00:03:01,383
Every lab runs in containers with synthetic findings and

51
00:03:01,383 --> 00:03:04,755
synthetic traffic. You will break rules on purpose,

52
00:03:04,755 --> 00:03:06,607
see the gate catch a bypass,

53
00:03:06,607 --> 00:03:09,715
and roll a mitigation back under time pressure.

54
00:03:12,715 --> 00:03:15,126
Here is the full table of contents,

55
00:03:15,126 --> 00:03:16,917
9 modules over three days.

56
00:03:16,917 --> 00:03:21,327
Day one: Virtual patching fundamentals and the agentic baseline;

57
00:03:21,327 --> 00:03:23,876
Finding ingestion and evidence model;

58
00:03:23,876 --> 00:03:26,081
and Context collection. Day two:

59
00:03:26,081 --> 00:03:30,697
Agentic mitigation planning; Constrained candidate rule generation;

60
00:03:30,697 --> 00:03:33,246
and Test harness and validation gate.

61
00:03:33,246 --> 00:03:36,759
Day three: Approval package and staging deployment;

62
00:03:36,759 --> 00:03:40,204
Monitoring, rollback and operations; and Capstone:

63
00:03:40,204 --> 00:03:43,029
end-to-end virtual patching lab platform.

64
00:03:46,029 --> 00:03:51,085
Every build in this course follows six engineering principles.

65
00:03:51,085 --> 00:03:53,286
Model output is a proposal,

66
00:03:53,286 --> 00:03:57,527
never a fact. Authorization lives outside the model.

67
00:03:57,527 --> 00:04:01,115
A human approves every consequential action.

68
00:04:01,115 --> 00:04:03,887
Decisions and evidence are logged.

69
00:04:03,887 --> 00:04:08,698
The stack stays provider-agnostic. And quality is measured,

70
00:04:08,698 --> 00:04:09,677
not assumed.

71
00:04:12,677 --> 00:04:14,931
Nine build steps. Three days,

72
00:04:14,931 --> 00:04:17,341
hands-on. Four classes of test.

73
00:04:17,341 --> 00:04:20,295
And zero deployments without approval.

74
00:04:23,295 --> 00:04:27,876
This course is for application security and product security

75
00:04:27,876 --> 00:04:31,313
engineers, DevSecOps, WAF and platform teams,

76
00:04:31,313 --> 00:04:35,436
and vulnerability management leads. You need basic H T

77
00:04:35,436 --> 00:04:39,025
T P, web security, Python and container skills.

78
00:04:42,025 --> 00:04:45,492
Close the gap between the finding and the fix.

79
00:04:45,492 --> 00:04:48,357
The Agentic Virtual Patching Platform.

80
00:04:48,357 --> 00:04:50,543
Enrol now at gennoor dot com.
